      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🩺 Uptime Monitor — the Conduit app from Task 1\n**Every 5 minutes** GET the frontend and the API; anything other than **HTTP 200** is DOWN.\n\n**Retry logic:** the HTTP node tries 3× (5 s apart) before a check counts as DOWN → no alerts for one-off blips.\n**Response time:** measured per target (stamp → request → measure) inside a one-at-a-time loop.\n**Daily summary** at 09:00 IST: uptime %, avg / p95 / max response time, incidents, minutes down.\n\nTest hooks (header `X-Webhook-Token`): `GET /webhook/uptime-check`, `GET /webhook/uptime-report`",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "5a6b7c8d-0501-4e5f-8a9b-000000000501",
      "name": "Note: overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        -448
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 🔔 Alert on changes, not on every check\n🔴 **DOWN** once · 🔴 reminder every **30 min** while still down · 🟢 **RECOVERED** with the downtime.\n\n**State** (up/down, last alert, stats) is kept in the n8n **Data Table** `uptime_state`, read at run time, and production runs are serialized (`N8N_CONCURRENCY_PRODUCTION_LIMIT=1`). Testing showed that workflow static data is snapshotted when a run is created, so two overlapping checks both alerted — this design fixes that.",
        "height": 270,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
